<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
  <section xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-08-better-interaction">
    <title>Improving Interaction</title>
    <introduction>
    <p>
        With the current interaction, when a crystal is collected or damaged, it just disappears.
        In the case of collection, it would make more sense if the collector brought the crystal
        back to the ship. For damage, it would make more sense if the ship were deflected in addition
        to the crystal disappearing, and perhaps the crystal should break apart before disappearing.
    </p>
    </introduction>
    <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-better-interaction-boomerang-collection">
      <title>Boomerang Collection</title>
      <p>
        For collection, we want the prize to be owned by the collector, and then we want both 
        the collector and prize to shrink as the collector moves to the ship. Then once the
        prize and ship collide, we want the prize to be collected and the collector to disappear.
      </p>
      <paragraphs>
        <title>Prize Changes</title>
        <p>We start with the prize.gd script. Since the prize handles all of the basic interactions
            we'll need to update the prize's collection steps. Since the prize will be moved from 
            the main scene to the collector scene, we'll add a member variable for the collector that 
            is holding the current prize, and also a member variable on collector of the prize 
            that the collector is holding. First, in prize.gd we'll add the collector that collected the
            prize as well as an indicator that the prize has been collected, so it is <c>inert</c> and 
            can't be collected again or change it's Sprite2D or value through growth.
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
        var collector: GrowingArea
        var inert: bool = false
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            Next, we need to update the behavior for collection. Instead of sending a signal and freeing
            itself, the prize needs to set inert to true, add the collector to it, and call collector.collect
            so that the collector can do the rest of the work. So, we find the check for if the collector 
            can collect in <c>check_touching_collectors()</c> of prize.gd and change all of the steps
            in the case when the collector can collect.
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
        if collector.can_collect(self.global_position):
            inert = true
            self.collector = collector
            collector.collect(self)
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            Before adding the collect method to the collector, we need to make sure that all of relevant 
            methods are disabled when inert is true. First, in <c>_process()</c> let the parent's _process
            happen, but skip the rest
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
func _process(delta: float) -> void:
    super._process(delta)
    ## add this code right after super._process()
    if inert:
        return
     ## keep the rest of the code as it was
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            Next, change the first line in <c>_on_area_entered()</c> to make sure
            inert is false in addition to the area being in the collector group.:
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
func _on_area_entered(area: Area2D) -> void:
    if not inert and area.is_in_group("collector"):
            </code>
        </program>
        <p>
            Next, change <c>_on_body_entered()</c> so that when it's not inert
            it still emits the hit signal, but otherwise it should emit the 
            collected signal, because that is when the collector has brought the 
            prize to the ship. In addition, if the prize has a collector, then
            that should be freed as well. The below is a wholesale change of the 
            _on_body_entered method in prize.gd.
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
func _on_body_entered(body: Node2D) -> void:
    if body.is_in_group("player"):
        if not inert:
            emit_signal("hit",value)
        else:
            emit_signal("collected",value)
        queue_free()
        if collector != null:
            collector.queue_free()
            </code>
        </program>
      </paragraphs>
      <paragraphs>
        <title>Collector Changes</title>
        <p>
            Now, we go to the collector.gd script and add a prize member variable, and then create the 
            collect method that is called by the prize as it's collected. In order for the collector to 
            go back to the ship after it encircles a prize, it needs to know the location of the ship,
            so a member variable for the ship as a source of the lasso is also needed.
        </p>
        <p>First the new member variables:
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
var prize: GrowingArea
var source: RigidBody2D
            </code>
            </program>
             <p>
                Next, the collect method takes the prize and assigns it as well as
                changing the grow rates so that both the collector and 
                prizes shrink to good sizes. In addition the hit stream needs to play 
                based on the collect state signal instead of the player's collect method, 
                and a separate collect stream and sound
                will be played when the player actually collects the prize.
                First we add <p>collect()</p> to the collector:
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
func collect(prize: GrowingArea) -> void:
    growth_rate = -0.2
    self.prize = prize
    if self.prize.current_scale &lt; self.prize.thresholds[0]:
        self.prize.growth_rate = -0.1
        emit_signal("collect_state",CollectState.HIT_SMALL)
    elif self.prize.current_scale &lt; self.prize.thresholds[1]:
        self.prize.growth_rate = -0.25
        emit_signal("collect_state",CollectState.HIT_MED)
    else:
        self.prize.growth_rate = -0.4
        emit_signal("collect_state",CollectState.HIT_LARGE)
    
    self.prize.start_growth()
            </code>
            </program>
            </paragraphs>
            <paragraphs>
                <title>Player Changes</title>
                <p>In the <c>launch()</c> method we need to assign the player 
                    as the source for each collector, so after instantiating the collector
                    add the following code:
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
collector.source = self
            </code>
            </program>
        
             <p>Then we add playing the hit stream to the player's receive_signal method
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
    elif coll_state in [Collector.CollectState.HIT_SMALL,
                        Collector.CollectState.HIT_MED,
                        Collector.CollectState.HIT_LARGE]:
        $SoundEffect.stream = collectorHitStream
        $SoundEffect.play()
            </code>
            </program>
             <p>Then we add a prize collected stream as a member variable of player.gd
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
var playerCollectedStream: AudioStream = load("res://sound/effects/prize_collected_quieter.ogg")
            </code>
            </program>
             <p>Then in player.gd <c>collect()</c> change the sound effect stream to be the playerCollectedStream:
        </p>
        <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
    $SoundEffect.stream = playerCollectedStream
            </code>
        </program>
      </paragraphs>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-better-interaction-bouncing-damage">
      <title>Damage Deflection</title>
      <p>
        When the ship hits a crystal and it gets destroyed, we also want the ship to be deflected. For this
        we cam use <c>apply_central_impulse</c> as shown below. Find the <c>_on_body_entered()</c>
        method in prize.gd and after <c>emit_signal("hit",value)</c> put the following code 
        at the same indentation level.
      </p>
      <program language="gdscript">
            <code>
var rigid: RigidBody2D = body as RigidBody2D
rigid.apply_central_impulse(-0.1*value*rigid.linear_velocity)
            </code>
        </program>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-better-interaction-playtesting">
      <title>Play Testing</title>
      <p>
        Now, test the upgraded interactions and make changes to any variables that will improve the experience.
      </p>
      </subsection>
    </section>
